  "answer": "Under the CUSB ordinance, a shortage of attendance can lead to both outcomes.  According to the attendance provisions (Source 2), if a student’s attendance falls below the prescribed limit, the student may be debarred from appearing in the examination or have the grade rejected.  Additionally, the ordinance’s removal clause (Source 3) states that a student who has failed to attend the classes as stipulated under the attendance requirements will have their name automatically struck off the rolls of the University.  Therefore, attendance shortage can result in exam debarment and, if it persists, in removal from the program."
